          "filename": "Sandhill cranes at Stone Lakes NWR (5347298450).jpg",
          "caption": "The Stone Lakes National Wildlife Refuge is south of Sacramento in the northern reaches of the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta.  FWS staff and partners have been working to restore historic wetland communities and enhance existing habitats in the 6,000-acre complex of wetland, riparian and grassland habitats. Stone Lakes NWR  provides wintering and migrating habitat for waterfowl, shorebirds and sandhill cranes each year, as well as breeding habitat for wood ducks, mallards and cinnamon teal.(Justine Belson/USFWS)",
          "alt": "The Stone Lakes National Wildlife Refuge is south of Sacramento in the northern reaches of the Sacramento-San Joaquin River Delta.  FWS staff and partners have been working to restore historic wetland communities and enhance existing habitats in the 6,000-acre complex of wetland, riparian and grassland habitats. Stone Lakes NWR  provides wintering and migrating habitat for waterfowl, shorebirds and sandhill cranes each year, as well as breeding habitat for wood ducks, mallards and cinnamon teal.(Justine Belson/USFWS)",
